#{[17592186385582 #edb/ref 1080 "11x-7y-z+2=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385582 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385582 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "28f3efb2-a8a3-5292-965f-156e973895f7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385583 #edb/ref 1080 "7x-11y+z+2=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385583 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385583 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2e0114f8-20c1-562a-b2e7-a7011c766d5c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385584 #edb/ref 1080 "11x-7y+z+4=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385584 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385584 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5bf255fb-dec1-53cd-ad7d-7500bd87d32a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403710 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403711 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403710 #edb/ref 1069 "q-73860" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403710 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403710 #edb/ref 1071 "At which points on the surface $z={x}^{3}-3x+{y}^{2}+2y$ is the tangent plane horizontal?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403710 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "14749651-a6a1-55fa-b209-fec427b8a368" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403710 #edb/ref 1074 "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhere $⟨\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),-1⟩$ represents a normal vector to the tangent plane.\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}-3x+{y}^{2}+2y) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}-3 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{3}-3x+{y}^{2}+2y) \\\\  & =2y+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nHence, the normal vector to the tangent plane is \n\n$$\n⟨3{x}^{2}-3,\\,2y+2,\\,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nNote that the tangent plane is horizontal if and only if the normal vector is vertical. This means that the $x$- and $y$-components of the vector must be $0:$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=0 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-3=0 \\\\ 2y+2=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the first equation, we get $x=\\pm 1$ while the second equation gives $y=-1.$ \n\nFinally, substituting $x=-1$ and $y=-1$ into our function, we get\n\n$$\nz=(-1)^{3}-3(-1)+(-1)^{2}+2(-1)=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=1$ and $y=-1$ into our function, we get\n\n$$\nz=(1)^{3}-3(1)+(-1)^{2}+2(-1)=-3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points where the tangent plane is horizontal are $(-1,-1,1)$ and $(1,-1,-3).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403711 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403712 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403711 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403713 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403711 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403714 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403711 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403715 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403711 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403711 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403711 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403711 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186403712 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403711 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "29a46a2f-b76d-5223-bfa0-caee05f36438" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403712 #edb/ref 1080 "$(-1,-1,1)$ and $(1,-1,-3)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403712 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403712 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "90f4afcf-4af1-5320-a876-c7e43193b7cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403713 #edb/ref 1080 "$(1,-1,-3)$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403713 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403713 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "aaeb48d9-f69d-5b9e-9626-640bfefc395e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403714 #edb/ref 1080 "$(1,1,0)$ and $(-1,1,2)$" #edb/re